## Troubleshooting Checklist

| Issue | Check |
|-------|-------|
| Calls not arriving | Verify Origination SIP URI points to your LiveKit server |
| "Trunk not found" | Ensure **Allowed Addresses** includes Twilio signaling IPs |
| 407 Unauthorized | Remove Username/Password from inbound trunk (use IP auth instead) |
| One-way audio | Verify **Symmetric RTP** is enabled in Twilio (Step 2) |
| No room created | Check dispatch rule is linked to correct trunk ID |
| Firewall blocked | Ensure TCP/UDP port 5060 is open for Twilio IPs in your cloud provider firewall (AWS Security Groups, GCP Firewall, etc.) |
| Outbound calls failing | Verify your server IP is in the Termination IP Access Control List |
| DNS resolution error / "no such host" | Ensure the Address includes a region (e.g., `.pstn.sydney.twilio.com` not `.pstn.twilio.com`). Check for typos like double dots (`..`) |
| Wrong caller ID | Check **Numbers** field in outbound trunk configuration |

